# Environment profiles of the .NET probe, one variable per line: `<arm> <NAME=value>`.
#
# Arm a is the base profile. Arm b is arm a plus the variables listed under `b`. `@DOTNET_ROOT@` stands for the directory
# that holds the dotnet executable. The probe is run as `$DOTNET_ROOT/dotnet LangAtProbe.dll`, with exactly these
# variables added to an otherwise minimal environment. profile-env.sh prints the words of an arm; test_probe.sh pins the
# lists below, so a change here fails the test until the test is changed too.
#
# Nothing else is set: no other DOTNET_* variable, and no runtime option in LangAtProbe.runtimeconfig.json.
a DOTNET_ROOT=@DOTNET_ROOT@
b DOTNET_TieredCompilation=0
b DOTNET_EnableWriteXorExecute=0
b DOTNET_gcServer=0
b DOTNET_PROCESSOR_COUNT=1
